4. libjpeg (the Independent JPEG Group's licence)

   packages/twk_rich/lib/src/image/jpeg.dart
     The JPEG decoder's integer IDCT (_idct, from jpeg_idct_islow in
     jidctint.c), its YCbCr to RGB tables (from build_ycc_rgb_table in
     jdcolor.c) and its refinement of progressive AC coefficients
     (_Decoder._refineAc, from decode_mcu_AC_refine in jdphuff.c) are
     translated from libjpeg, compared with libjpeg-turbo 3.2.0
     (https://github.com/libjpeg-turbo/libjpeg-turbo/tree/3.2.0). This
     software is based in part on the work of the Independent JPEG Group.

   packages/twk_rich/README.ijg
     libjpeg-turbo 3.2.0's README.ijg, whole and unaltered, as the IJG's
     licence asks of a distribution of any part of its source code.

   Copyright (C) 1991-2020, Thomas G. Lane, Guido Vollbeding, and the
   copyright notices of those files. packages/twk_rich/NOTICE names
   each part's file and lines and what was changed, and carries the
   licence. It applies to an executable only where it imports
   package:twk_rich/image.dart, the one library that reaches jpeg.dart:
   package:twk_rich/twk_rich.dart neither exports nor imports it.


5. jpgjs: pdf.js (Apache License 2.0) and package:image (MIT License)

   packages/twk_rich/lib/src/image/jpeg.dart
     The decoder's walk through a scan's MCUs (_Decoder._scan), its
     decoding of baseline, DC and first AC blocks (_Decoder._block, modes
     0 to 3) and its colour transform of three components follow jpgjs,
     as pdf.js v4.10.38 keeps it in src/core/jpg.js
     (https://github.com/mozilla/pdf.js/blob/v4.10.38/src/core/jpg.js)
     and as package:image 4.5.4 ports it to Dart in
     lib/src/formats/jpeg/jpeg_scan.dart and jpeg_frame.dart
     (https://github.com/brendan-duncan/image/tree/4.5.4/lib/src/formats/jpeg),
     changed for this decoder.

   pdf.js's jpg.js: Copyright 2014 Mozilla Foundation; jpgjs: Copyright
   (C) 2011 notmasteryet; both under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
   package:image: Copyright (c) 2013-2022 Brendan Duncan, under the MIT
   License. packages/twk_rich/NOTICE names each part's files and lines
   and what was changed, and carries both licences. They apply to an
   executable only where it imports package:twk_rich/image.dart, as in
   item 4.


